/-!
# Critical enstrophy envelope on arbitrary generated shell paths

The energy-level endpoint geometry carries the three-dimensional weight
`shellCard / shellSq`.  That weight grows with the highest generated
frequency and therefore cannot by itself give a cutoff-independent endpoint
Serrin estimate.

This module makes the PDE-selected reweighting explicit.  One more factor of
the exact shell is assigned to the vorticity amplitude, where it is precisely
the Fourier density of `|nabla omega|^2`.  The geometric factor becomes

```text
shellCard / shellSq^2.
```

For every source-generated finite path this yields a pointwise velocity
bound by a reciprocal-fourth-power lattice kernel times the exact
shell-weighted vorticity mass.  No cutoff, path length, amplitude decay,
time window, viscosity budget, or continuation certificate is accepted as a
premise.  A downstream lattice theorem and the actual enstrophy ledger must
still pay the global summability and time-integrated dissipation costs.
-/

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace NavierStokes
namespace ThreeDimensionalVorticityCoefficientGeneratedPathCriticalEnvelope

open scoped BigOperators Matrix

open ThreeDimensionalPeriodicCoarseFilterCore
open ThreeDimensionalPeriodicIntegerCharacterCoarseFilter
